Implement the Cinema City schedule adapter:

1. Fetch `/tickets/Movies`.
2. Fetch `/tickets/Events` for each movie and requested date.
3. Filter events to the requested cinema.
4. Convert them to the normalized `Screening` model.
5. Register the adapter in `app/adapters/registry.py`.
6. Make `GET /api/screenings?date=YYYY-MM-DD` return real Cinema City results.
7. Add tests using mocked HTTP responses; tests must not depend on live cinema sites.

## Seat retrieval update (2026-09-14)

`GET /api/screenings/{screening_id}/seats` resolves the ID returned by schedules
and fetches seats on demand, without refetching schedules or storing screenings.
Unknown IDs/branches and missing provider events return 404; provider/schema
failures and the 60-second overall deadline return 502.

Cinema City, Yes Planet, and Lev use shared PresGlobal retrieval: initialize an
anonymous UUID with GET `/order/{id}`, fetch `/api/presentations/{id}`, POST the
read-only `/api/seats/seatplanV2`, and GET `/api/seats/seats-statusV2`.
The UUID/cookies exist only for that request. No booking scripts are executed.
Status keys identify available seats; missing keys mean unavailable, not
necessarily occupied. Rotation and group offsets are applied to coordinates.

Hot Cinema and Movieland share `BiggerPictureSession`. Their event response
contains the layout (`vsp.vsedl[].vssedl`); the separate status feed reports sold
and held seats. Deleted layout cells are excluded. An empty successful status
feed means no reported sold/held seats only when paired with a valid layout.
No cart creation, seat selection, holds, or purchases are performed.

SeatMap includes section IDs, display row/seat labels, coordinates, seat kinds,
status counts (available, occupied, held, unavailable, unknown), and fetched_at.
Occupied means explicitly reported sold seats; do not interpret zero occupied
as a verified empty auditorium for PresGlobal. Occupancy percentage and central
seat-pair recommendations remain future work. Coordinates use provider units;
Bigger Picture coordinates are local to each section.

Live read checks on 2026-09-14 succeeded for Cinema City (33 seats), Planet
(394), Hot Cinema (82), and Movieland (85), one screening each. Lev status reads
succeeded, but its layout POST returned 403 even after session initialization.
Lev's integration is implemented and mock-tested, but live retrieval remains
blocked by that provider response and returns 502. Do not claim live seat support
for Lev until its layout request succeeds. The cause of the 403 is unconfirmed.
